# fixedbugs, defect 2286, 2026-11-08 (panel 236's R3): a value made from one
# module's `extern` crosses to C through another module's. A value keeps C's
# convention, so the `extern` stands as itself and no adapter has to be one
# function across units; the proposal as first written refused this program at
# build. `fixedbugs_2286_call_ret` reads the record's first word and its last.
use caller
use holder

function main()
    f = holder.maker()
    print(caller.hand(cb: f, n: 5))
    print(f(6).first)
